[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706134350","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706134350","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706134350,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hTFVO","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T10:49:07Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T10:49:41Z","body":"Isn't mapping physical inputs to semantic ones the whole point of actions? \r\nI'm not opposed to the underlying idea, I just feel we're reinventing the wheel and mixing comcerns here","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706134350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706651810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706651810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706651810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVDqi","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T14:53:43Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T14:53:43Z","body":"> Isn't mapping physical inputs to semantic ones the whole point of actions? \n\nYes, and in most cases this is sufficient.\n\nThe issue arises when the same physical input _means something different_ depending on which controller is in use.\n\nSpecifically, Xbox controller users expect the bottom face button to act as \"yes,\" whereas Nintendo controller users expect it to act as \"no.\" (And vice versa for the right face button.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706651810/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706705044","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706705044","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706705044,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVQqU","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T15:14:02Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T15:14:02Z","body":"I ser your point now. I feel this might be addressed in a way that's more in line with the current way input works, by allowing defining a different physical input to an action based on controller type. \r\n\r\nSo for example, you create an accept action bound to Nintendo A and Xbox A, instead of mapping to generic \"button 1\".  I imagine this would work similarly to choosing between physical and vs keycode when adding a keyboard input. \r\n\r\nThis way the semantics stay on the side of the action, while allowing different configurations for each platform. \r\n\r\nHow does that sound? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706705044/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706755621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706755621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706755621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVdAl","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T15:35:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T15:35:46Z","body":"> I ser your point now. I feel this might be addressed in a way that's more in line with the current way input works, by allowing defining a different physical input to an action based on controller type. \n\nThat might be another possibility, though I worry it may be a bit over-engineered.\n\nReally the only scenario this PR currently seeks to address is the discrepancy in `A` & `B` buttons, and I think the complexity of providing per-controller-type events would be overkill for this case.\n\nIs there another use case you have in mind for segregated input events?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706755621/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706770765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706770765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706770765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVgtN","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T15:42:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T15:42:35Z","body":"I don't have a use case right now, but it makes me wonder how common it would be for games to map input differently per-console.\r\n\r\n For example the convention for jumping being different between switch and playstation (making this up)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706770765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706889204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706889204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706889204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hV9n0","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T16:27:47Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T16:27:47Z","body":"> I don't have a use case right now, but it makes me wonder how common it would be for games to map input differently per-console.\r\n\r\nAs far as I'm aware, all other controls are typically mapped to the same physical position.\r\n\r\nI checked some popular games from other engines to see how they handle it:\r\n\r\n- [Hollow Knight](https://hollowknight.wiki/w/Controls_(Hollow_Knight)) (Unity) maps all gameplay controls positionally but uses the expected `A`/`B` mappings for menu actions on each console.\r\n- [Fortnite](https://fortnite.fandom.com/wiki/Controls) (Unreal) similarly seems to map all gameplay controls positionally but use the native `A`/`B` menu actions.\r\n- [Minecraft Bedrock Ed.](https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/article/minecraft-controls) (custom C++ engine) maps everything positionally except for `A`/`B`, which it maps according to platform (for both menu and gameplay actions).\r\n\r\nEven if we were to find another common case of differing conventions, it should be fairly trivial to extend it from this PR.\r\nI don't foresee a significant number of these (if any), so I don't think it makes sense to preemptively accommodate them.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706889204/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706901238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2706901238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2706901238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hWAj2","user":{"login":"JoNax97","id":10124534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10124534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97","html_url":"https://github.com/JoNax97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoNax97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T16:33:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T16:33:23Z","body":"Makes sense to me","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706901238/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707242118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744#issuecomment-2707242118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","id":2707242118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hXTyG","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T19:27:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T19:27:57Z","body":"Now based on #89193 and its controller type detection","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707242118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimiz